    "context7": "Resolved /llvm/llvm-project then fetched LLD RELRO/page-size documentation (2commands); inspected official bionic/LLD sources for loader rounding and segment separation."
  },
  "conclusion": "No GNU_RELRO rounding collision in any of the 8 packaged 64-bit libraries. In 5 nonaligned logical-end cases, rounding covers only safe padding before the next writable LOAD page; 3 end aligned. No writable allocated section or PF_W LOAD memory outside logical RELRO intersects rounded protection.",
  "runtime_unknown": "No 16 KiB runtime was tested. This establishes static RELRO/layout compatibility only; unrelated runtime page-size assumptions remain unqualified.",
  "review_correction": "Supersedes the earlier receipt/README wording that nonaligned logical RELRO ends themselves require review/rebuild; actual section/segment layout shows no writable-data overlap.",
  "source_analysis": {
    "bionic": "_phdr_table_set_gnu_relro_prot uses page_start(p_vaddr) and page_end(p_vaddr+p_memsz), then mprotect. Its _extend_gnu_relro_prot_end guard avoids extending protection when the containing LOAD also has writable non-RELRO contents. For these separate-LOAD layouts, the next writable LOAD page begins at the already-rounded RELRO end.",
    "lld": "Official linker-script documentation describes separation of RELRO from following writable PT_LOAD ranges; actual LLD18/19 producer comments and binary layouts were recorded rather than assuming a required modulo-zero logical end.",
    "guide_interpretation": "The Android guide modulo test is a conservative warning. Nonzero modulo is not sufficient evidence of failure when the rounded page contains no writable data outside RELRO. This audit checks the actual condition directly.",
    "scope": "Current official bionic main/source documentation was reviewed; this does not execute every Android loader release. Producer fork sources were not downloaded. Static binary intersections provide the artifact-specific result."
  }
}
